('CIT_MES_DUMUZI_TAMMUZ_ETCSL','ENT_MES_DUMUZI_TAMMUZ','SRC_ETCSL','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','2.02, line 36 nam nun-e saj na-il2 X nam-lugal The Sumerian king list, 2.1.1 cag4-ga-a-ni Dumuzid''s dream, 1.4.3 an gal-ta ki gal-ce3 Inana''s descent to the nether world, 1.4.1 ud re-a nam ba-tar- ra Enki''s journey to Nibru, 1.1.4 ud re-a ud sud4-ta re -a two compositions are known with this incipit: Gilgame&c;, Enkidu and the nether world, 1.8.1.4 and The instructions of &C;uruppag, 5.6.1 ud re-a nij2-ul-e UD MA DAM-DAM NA-NA di4-di4-la2 ud-da Dialogue 2,','Black, Cunningham, Robson, Zólyomi et al.',2006,'https://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Located by name in the ETCSL translations; verify the composition (c.x.x) reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MES_IGIGI_ETCSL','ENT_MES_IGIGI','SRC_ETCSL','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','The great-hearted mistress, the impetuous lady, proud among the Anuna gods and pre-eminent in all lands, the great daughter of Suen , exalted among the Great Princes a name of the Igigi gods , the magnificent lady who gathers up the divine powers of heaven and earth and rivals great An , is mightiest among the great gods -- she makes their verdicts final.','Black, Cunningham, Robson, Zólyomi et al.',2006,'https://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Located by name in the ETCSL translations; verify the composition (c.x.x) reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
