('CIT_MES_NUSKA_ETCSL','ENT_MES_NUSKA','SRC_ETCSL','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','Electronic Text Corpus of Sumerian Literature (ETCSL)','Good minister, I shall praise you! Nuska , majestic minister of Enlil , your praise is good and most sweet. My king, I shall praise you in song! You are the light of the good shepherd Enlil , and you have been given a majestic name by Ninlil . You have been given wisdom by Enki . You were born to Enul and Ninul , and so you are united with the lordly seed. You are the E-kur''s song.','Black, Cunningham, Robson, Zólyomi et al.',2006,'https://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Located by name in the ETCSL translations; verify the composition (c.x.x) reference.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1)
